diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 3074883..e6be8de 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -90,3 +90,17 @@ Quizzy is a Rails 8.1 application using SQLite (`storage/*.sqlite3`), Propshaft
     - `"Top <N>"` (`POST /moderate/quizzes/:quiz_id/games/:id/top_winners`): selects the first N players on the leaderboard with `points > 0`.
     - `"Draw"` (`POST /moderate/quizzes/:quiz_id/games/:id/draw_winners`): awards prizes to all players with strictly more points than N-th place, and draws the remaining prizes at random among players tied with N-th place's points (excluding 0-point players). Each click draws again.
     - `"Reset winners"` (`POST /moderate/quizzes/:quiz_id/games/:id/reset_winners`): clears all winners.
+
+## Question Timer (Release 5)
+- **Quiz Settings**:
+  - `Quiz#timer_minutes` (`quizzes.timer_minutes`, integer, `default: 0`, validated `>= 0`).
+  - `Quiz#timer_seconds` (`quizzes.timer_seconds`, integer, `default: 0`, validated `>= 0`).
+  - Editable via `"Timer minutes"` and `"Timer seconds"` fields in Quiz Settings (`/moderate/quizzes/:id/edit`) and New Quiz form.
+  - `0` minutes and `0` seconds disables the timer (`quiz.timer_enabled? == false`).
+  - Not included in the quiz JSON export format.
+- **Live Countdown & Auto-Finish**:
+  - When a question opens (`start!` or `next_question!`), `question_opened_at` is persisted on `Game`.
+  - Deadline is `question_opened_at + quiz.timer_total_seconds.seconds`. Reloading the moderator's big screen calculates remaining time from `question_opened_at`, so the countdown never restarts on reload.
+  - While `question_open?` and `quiz.timer_enabled?`, the moderator's big screen displays `#question-timer` in `M:SS` format (`"1:30"`, `"0:05"`, etc.), updated every 50ms client-side. Players never see the timer.
+  - At `0:00`, `GameTimer` (server-side background thread) and `Game#finish_if_timer_expired!` (also checked on state/answer requests) atomically transition the question from `question_open` to `question_closed` and broadcast to the big screen and all players, just as if the moderator clicked `"Finish"`.
+  - Clicking `"Finish"` earlier cancels `GameTimer` and closes the question immediately.
